# Notification Category Filters

## Summary
Add category filtering to the full `/notifications` page only. Keep the existing `All / Unread / Read` status tabs, and add a separate category filter for `Appraisal`, `KPI`, `360 Feedback`, `One-on-one Meeting`, `PIP`, and `Self-Assessment`. Filters should be backend-backed so pagination totals and pages stay correct.

## Key Changes
- Backend `/api/notifications`:
  - Add optional query params: `status=all|unread|read` and `source=<source>`.
  - Validate `source` against: `APPRAISAL`, `KPI`, `360_FEEDBACK`, `MEETING`, `PIP`, `SELF_ASSESSMENT_FORM`.
  - Use repository-level filtering, preferably with `JpaSpecificationExecutor<Notification>`, so filtering applies before pagination.
  - Keep `/unread-count` unchanged as the global unread count.

- Frontend `/notifications` page:
  - Extend `useGetNotificationsQuery` params with `status` and `source`.
  - Replace current client-side filtering with server-side params.
  - Keep status tabs: `All`, `Unread`, `Read`.
  - Add a separate category control with: `All Categories`, `Appraisal`, `KPI`, `360 Feedback`, `One-on-one Meeting`, `PIP`, `Self-Assessment`.
  - Reset page to `0` whenever status or category changes.
  - Use friendly source labels instead of raw `replaceAll('_', ' ')`.

- Notification navigation:
  - Keep existing routes for `360_FEEDBACK`, `MEETING`, and `SELF_ASSESSMENT_FORM`.
  - Add source-aware destinations for `PIP`, `APPRAISAL`, and `KPI` so current/future notifications do not fall back to 360 Feedback.
  - Use role prefix from current path:
    - `PIP`: HR -> `/hr/pip-monitoring`, Manager -> `/manager/pip`, Employee -> `/employee/pip`
    - `APPRAISAL`: HR -> `/hr/appraisals`, Manager -> `/manager/appraisals`, Employee fallback -> `/employee/dashboard`
    - `KPI`: HR -> `/hr/kpi-management`, Manager -> `/manager/kpis`, Employee -> `/employee/kpis`

## Test Plan
- Backend:
  - Add or update notification service/controller tests for `status`, `source`, combined status+source, invalid status, invalid source, and pagination totals.
- Frontend:
  - Add focused tests for `/notifications` query params changing when status/category changes.
  - Verify page resets to `0` on filter changes.
  - Verify empty-state text and friendly labels for category filters.
- Manual verification:
  - Build frontend with `npm run build`.
  - Run backend tests related to notifications if available.
  - Check `/hr/notifications`, `/manager/notifications`, and `/employee/notifications`.

## Assumptions
- Do not modify the notification bell popover.
- Do not create new Appraisal or KPI notification emitters in this task; the filters will work once notifications with `APPRAISAL` or `KPI` sources exist.
- `One-on-one Meeting` maps to the existing backend source `MEETING`.
- `Self-Assessment` maps to the existing backend source `SELF_ASSESSMENT_FORM`.
